# EMU Alerts Clean - Project Intelligence

## Project Overview
This is the EMU Alerts Clean project - a fresh alert notification system for EMU (Eastern Michigan University or EMU system). The project is in its initial setup phase with comprehensive memory bank documentation established.

## Memory Bank Structure
This project uses a comprehensive Memory Bank system located in `/memory-bank/`:
- **CRITICAL**: Always read ALL memory bank files at the start of every session
- Core files: projectbrief.md, productContext.md, activeContext.md, systemPatterns.md, techContext.md, progress.md
- Memory bank is the single source of truth for project state and decisions

## Development Preferences
### Technology Stack (User Preferences)
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (always use pnpm over npm/yarn)
- **Framework**: Next.js with Turbopack for React projects
- **Testing**: Vitest (run tests before pushing changes)
- **Agent Mode**: Run terminal commands automatically with non-interactive flags (-y)
- **Build Tools**: Prefer Turbopack over Webpack for dev servers

### Development Workflow
- Always use absolute paths when possible
- Run commands automatically in Agent mode
- Iterate until tests are green before pushing
- Use Background Agents for long-running tasks
- Ship end-to-end: implementation, tests, and minimal docs

### Code Quality Standards
- Explain in plain English with step-by-step approach
- Use short code comments for clarity
- Maintain clean, documented codebase
- Default to safe commands; ask only if destructive
- Optimize for autonomy - minimize manual paste requests

## Project Patterns
### Fresh Repository Characteristics
- Started from completely empty repository
- No legacy code to work around
- Clean slate allows for modern architecture choices
- All decisions are new and need to be documented

### Documentation Strategy
- Memory Bank is comprehensive and must be maintained
- Update activeContext.md and progress.md frequently
- Document all architectural decisions in systemPatterns.md
- Keep techContext.md updated as stack evolves

### Architecture Philosophy
- Design for reliability (critical for alert systems)
- Plan for scalability from the start
- Security-first approach for user data
- Clean separation of concerns
- Event-driven architecture for alert processing

## Key Project Insights
- **Alert System Focus**: This is specifically for alert/notification management
- **University Context**: Likely needs integration with EMU systems
- **Reliability Critical**: Emergency alerts require high availability
- **Multi-channel**: Email, SMS, push notifications needed
- **User Management**: Both admin and end-user interfaces required

## Development Context
- **Environment**: Linux with bash shell
- **Starting Point**: Completely fresh - no existing codebase
- **Requirements Status**: Needs definition from stakeholders
- **Current Phase**: Project initialization and planning

